# Each place that gives an array storage for numbers counts the short-lived arrays it has done that for, and gives up when they are many. It gives up for itself: the operation stays at its place,
# however rare its block and however many functions hold the like of it. In one body for all of them, the loops over long-lived arrays would run their general copy for ever
# FORM: Selected
# OPTIONS: check=VerifyEachPass heat=OnlyLoopsAreHot
# RUN: pass OutlineColdOperations
# CHECK-NOT: role=OutlinedBody
# CHECK-COUNT-8: ConvertToDoubleStorage v0

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
# REPEAT: i = 0..7

function f%(i) name="reads%(i)" parameters=[{type=Array<number>}, {type=boolean}] results=[{type=undefined}] {
    Branch v1 -> taken b1(), notTaken b2()
  b1() frequency=Rare:
    ConvertToDoubleStorage v0
    Jump -> next b2()
  b2():
    Return
}
# END REPEAT
